## 8. CTA & Funnel Strategy

**Primary CTA:**
The action is: search for available apartments on brightplace.

Place the CTA in three locations:
1. After the opening answer paragraph (first H2), before the first category section. Framing: "If you are still deciding which apartments to tour, brightplace shows available units with pricing and floor plan details side by side, so you can build a tour list before you spend time in showings."
2. After the "Cost and Total Monthly Fees" H2 (mid-article). Framing: "brightplace tracks listed rent and fee structures across available apartments, making it easier to compare true monthly costs before you schedule a showing."
3. End of article, before FAQ. Framing: "Once you have your questions ready, find apartments worth touring at brightplace.ai."

CTA language must not use: "unlock," "leverage," "navigate," "explore" (in a promotional context). Use: "find," "see," "check," "compare."

**Secondary CTA:**
If brightplace has a published guide on apartment budgeting or first-time renter topics, link to it in the "How to Prepare Before the Tour" H2 with the framing: "For a breakdown of how to budget total monthly costs before signing, see [linked article title] on brightplace."

The writing agent should check the brightplace sitemap for the closest match to: apartment budgeting, first apartment checklist, or rent price guides by city. Use whichever is most directly relevant.

